<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ 'subscription.css' | asset_url }}">

{%- if product.selling_plan_groups.size > 0 -%}

{%- comment -%} Pass accent color from block settings into CSS variable {%- endcomment -%}
<style>
  #sub-widget-{{ block.id }} {
    --sub-accent: {{ block.settings.accent_color }};
    --sub-accent-light: {{ block.settings.accent_color }}18;
    --sub-border-active: {{ block.settings.accent_color }};
    --sub-bg-active: {{ block.settings.accent_color }}0f;
    --sub-shadow-active: 0 0 0 3px {{ block.settings.accent_color }}26;
  }

  {%- comment -%}
    Merchant CSS from the block's "Custom CSS" setting. Emitted last so it
    overrides subscription.css at equal specificity, since this tag already
    follows that stylesheet's link.

    Written raw rather than wrapped in a selector: merchants write complete
    rules, and wrapping would only allow bare property declarations.

    The replace filters are forgiveness, not security. Pasting a whole style
    element is common, and its closing tag would otherwise terminate this one
    early and spill the remainder onto the page as visible text. The needles are
    assembled with append because a literal closing style tag cannot appear
    inside a style element without ending it.

    strip_html is deliberately avoided: it strips everything between angle
    brackets and so would mangle valid CSS media queries that use a less-than
    comparison.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if block.settings.custom_css != blank -%}
  {%- assign style_close = '</' | append: 'style>' -%}
  {%- assign style_open  = '<'  | append: 'style>' -%}
  {{ block.settings.custom_css | replace: style_close, '' | replace: style_open, '' }}
  {%- endif -%}
</style>

{%- comment -%}
  Benefit chips, rendered here for the same reason as data-design below: this is
  the value that always works. The app can refine them per shop and per plan,
  but that arrives over the app proxy and is best-effort, so a chip row that
  depended on it alone stayed empty whenever the proxy was unreachable or the
  app was running older code.

  json-encoded per value rather than hand-quoted: chip text is merchant free
  text and would otherwise break the attribute on an apostrophe.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign chip_list = block.settings.benefit_1
  | append: '||' | append: block.settings.benefit_2
  | append: '||' | append: block.settings.benefit_3
  | split: '||' -%}
{%- capture theme_chips -%}
  {%- assign chip_sep = '' -%}
  [
  {%- for chip in chip_list -%}
    {%- assign trimmed = chip | strip -%}
    {%- if trimmed != blank -%}
      {{- chip_sep }}{{ trimmed | json -}}
      {%- assign chip_sep = ',' -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
  ]
{%- endcapture -%}

{%- comment -%}
  data-design is rendered here rather than fetched, so the layout is correct on
  first paint. The app admin (Settings → Widget designs) can still override it,
  but that override goes through the app proxy and is therefore best-effort;
  this is the value that always works.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- comment -%}
  Money formatting comes from Liquid rather than being inferred from the page.
  Scraping a rendered price for its currency symbol breaks on every locale that
  puts the symbol after the number ("10,00 €"), and silently fell back to "$" —
  a euro store rendered dollar prices in the widget while the rest of the page
  was correct. shop.money_format is always right and always available here.
{%- endcomment -%}
<div class="sub-widget" id="sub-widget-{{ block.id }}"
     data-design="{{ block.settings.design }}"
     data-theme-chips="{{ theme_chips | strip | escape }}"
     data-money-format="{{ shop.money_format | escape }}"
     data-currency="{{ cart.currency.iso_code | default: shop.currency | escape }}">

  {%- comment -%}
    Per-variant map of the selling plans actually allocated to each variant:
    { "<variantId>": { "<sellingPlanId>": <subscriptionPriceInCents>, ... }, ... }
    The JS uses this to only show a subscription for the variants it was assigned to.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <script type="application/json" class="sub-variant-plans">
  {
    {%- for variant in product.variants -%}
      "{{ variant.id }}": {
        {%- for alloc in variant.selling_plan_allocations -%}
          "{{ alloc.selling_plan.id }}": {{ alloc.price | default: variant.price }}{%- unless forloop.last -%},{%- endunless -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      }{%- unless forloop.last -%},{%- endunless -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
  }
  </script>

  {%- comment -%}
    The product's variants, straight from Liquid.

    The JS previously reached for window.ShopifyAnalytics.meta.product.variants,
    which is undocumented and absent whenever analytics is disabled or a consent
    app defers it — variant price updates then stopped working with no error. It
    also read a window.KAS_PRODUCT_DATA that nothing in this app ever set.
    Rendering the data here removes both dependencies.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <script type="application/json" class="sub-product-data">
  {{ product.variants | json }}
  </script>

  <p class="sub-widget__label">Purchase Options</p>

  <div class="sub-widget__options" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Purchase options">

    {%- comment -%} ONE-TIME PURCHASE {%- endcomment -%}
    <label class="sub-option sub-option--active" for="sub-onetime-{{ block.id }}">
      <input
        class="sub-option__radio"
        type="radio"
        id="sub-onetime-{{ block.id }}"
        name="sub_purchase_option_{{ block.id }}"
        value=""
        autocomplete="off"
        checked
      />
      <span class="sub-option__inner">
        <span class="sub-option__left">
          <span class="sub-option__dot"></span>
          <span class="sub-option__title">One-time purchase</span>
        </span>
        <span class="sub-option__price" data-base-price="{{ product.selected_or_first_available_variant.price }}">
          {{ product.selected_or_first_available_variant.price | money }}
        </span>
      </span>
    </label>

    {%- comment -%} SUBSCRIPTION OPTIONS {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- for group in product.selling_plan_groups -%}
      {%- for plan in group.selling_plans -%}

        {%- assign base_price   = product.selected_or_first_available_variant.price -%}
        {%- assign discount_pct = 0 -%}
        {%- assign final_price  = base_price -%}

        {%- for adj in plan.price_adjustments -%}
          {%- if adj.value_type == 'percentage' -%}
            {%- assign discount_pct = adj.value -%}
            {%- assign discount_amt = base_price | times: discount_pct | divided_by: 100 -%}
            {%- assign final_price  = base_price | minus: discount_amt -%}
          {%- elsif adj.value_type == 'fixed_amount' -%}
            {%- assign final_price  = base_price | minus: adj.value -%}
          {%- elsif adj.value_type == 'price' -%}
            {%- assign final_price  = adj.value -%}
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}

        {%- comment -%}
          The interval label as the plan was created with it — "Every 10 Weeks".
          The benefits design lowercases it into "Delivery every 10 weeks" for its
          dropdown, so that reading never depends on how the merchant named the plan.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <label
          class="sub-option"
          for="sub-plan-{{ plan.id }}-{{ block.id }}"
          data-plan-id="{{ plan.id }}"
          data-plan-price="{{ final_price }}"
          data-discount="{{ discount_pct }}"
          data-plan-option="{{ plan.options.first.value | default: plan.name }}"
          data-group-id="{{ group.id }}"
        >
          <input
            class="sub-option__radio"
            type="radio"
            id="sub-plan-{{ plan.id }}-{{ block.id }}"
            name="sub_purchase_option_{{ block.id }}"
            value="{{ plan.id }}"
            autocomplete="off"
          />
          <span class="sub-option__inner">
            <span class="sub-option__left">
              <span class="sub-option__dot"></span>
              <span class="sub-option__title">
                {{ group.name }}
                {%- if discount_pct > 0 -%}
                  <span class="sub-option__badge">SAVE {{ discount_pct }}%</span>
                {%- endif -%}
              </span>
            </span>
            <span class="sub-option__price">
              {{ final_price | money }}
            </span>
          </span>
        </label>

      {%- endfor -%}
    {%- endfor -%}

  </div>

  {%- if block.settings.show_savings -%}
    <div class="sub-widget__savings" id="sub-savings-{{ block.id }}" aria-live="polite"></div>
  {%- endif -%}

</div>

{%- endif -%}

<script src="{{ 'subscription.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Subscription Options",
  "target": "section",
  "templates": ["product"],
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "design",
      "label": "Design",
      "info": "Overridden by Settings → Widget designs in the Smart Subscriptions app when that app is reachable.",
      "options": [
        { "value": "default",  "label": "Default — standard option list" },
        { "value": "arctic",   "label": "Arctic — save badge inline, frequency picker" },
        { "value": "ribbon",   "label": "Ribbon — save badge on a corner ribbon" },
        { "value": "benefits", "label": "Benefits — full-width picker with benefit chips" }
      ],
      "default": "arctic"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "accent_color",
      "label": "Accent color",
      "default": "#f97316"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_savings",
      "label": "Show savings callout",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Benefit chips",
      "info": "Shown by the Benefits design under the frequency picker. Use {discount} for the plan's discount — that chip is hidden automatically when a plan has none. The app can override these per shop and per plan; leave a field blank to drop that chip."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "benefit_1",
      "label": "Benefit chip 1",
      "default": "{discount}% off each order"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "benefit_2",
      "label": "Benefit chip 2",
      "default": "Manage subscriptions easily"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "benefit_3",
      "label": "Benefit chip 3",
      "default": "Earn loyalty points"
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "custom_css",
      "label": "Custom CSS",
      "info": "Write full CSS rules. Useful selectors: .sub-widget, .sub-option, .sub-option--active, .sub-option__title, .sub-option__price, .sub-option__badge, .sub-widget__savings. Benefits design: .sub-arctic__picker, .sub-arctic__select, .sub-arctic__compare, .sub-arctic__chips, .sub-arctic__chip"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}

